#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_captured_inject:2
msgid ""
"Runs a subprocess, capturing the output. Returns a list of whitespace-"
"separated strings of the stdout that was produced. The string is split using "
"xonsh's lexer, rather than Python's str.split() or shlex.split()."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_captured_object:2
msgid ""
"Runs a subprocess, capturing the output. Returns an instance of "
"CommandPipeline representing the completed command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_captured_stdout:2
msgid ""
"Runs a subprocess, capturing the output. Returns the stdout that was "
"produced as a str or list based on ``$XONSH_SUBPROC_OUTPUT_FORMAT``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_captured_stdout:5
msgid ""
"``in_boolop`` is set by the parser to True when this call is a direct "
"operand of a ``&&``/``||`` chain, so the runtime can adjust behavior (e.g. "
"suppress ``$XONSH_SUBPROC_CMD_RAISE_ERROR`` to let the chain short-circuit "
"on returncode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:2
msgid ""
"Raise ``CalledProcessError`` if *value* is the (final) result of a subproc "
"statement that ended in failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:5
msgid "Used as the AST wrapper around two kinds of nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:7
msgid ""
"The outermost ``BoolOp`` of a logical chain (``cmd1 && cmd2`` / ``cmd1 || "
"cmd2``).  Python ``and``/``or`` short-circuits to the pipeline that "
"determined the chain result, so the wrapper sees the *final* pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:11
msgid ""
"A standalone subproc-helper call at statement level — bare commands, ``!"
"[...]``, ``$[...]``, ``$(...)``, ``@$(...)``.  The explicit-capture form ``!"
"(...)`` is *intentionally* not wrapped: per spec it is the user's full "
"responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:16
msgid ""
"When ``$XONSH_SUBPROC_RAISE_ERROR`` is True (default), this enforces \"raise "
"on the last executed pipeline's non-zero exit code\" semantics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:19
msgid "``ls nono`` (standalone) — rc≠0: raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:20
msgid "``$(ls nono)`` (standalone) — rc≠0: raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:21
msgid "``$[ls nono]`` (standalone) — rc≠0: raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:22
msgid "``echo 1 && echo 2`` — last is ``echo 2`` (rc=0): no raise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:23
msgid "``ls nono || echo 1`` — last is ``echo 1`` (rc=0): no raise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:24
msgid "``ls nono && echo 1`` — last is ``ls nono`` (rc≠0): raises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:26
msgid "Per-command overrides:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:28
msgid ""
"``@error_ignore`` (``spec.raise_subproc_error is False``) on the final "
"pipeline suppresses the raise — used e.g. for ``echo 1 && @error_ignore ls "
"nono``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:31
msgid ""
"``@error_raise`` raises directly at the pipeline level, so the wrapper never "
"sees a failed value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_check_boolop:34
msgid ""
"Some subproc helpers (``$()``, ``$[]``, ``@$()``) return a *string* / "
"*None* / *list* rather than a ``CommandPipeline``, so the wrapper can't read "
"``returncode`` directly off ``value``.  In that case it falls back to ``XSH."
"lastcmd`` — the most recently completed pipeline, which is the one this "
"helper just ran."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../xonsh/built_ins.py:docstring of
#: xonsh.built_ins.subproc_uncaptured:2
msgid ""
"Runs a subprocess, without capturing the output. Returns the stdout that was "
"produced as a str."
msgstr ""

